content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-112 - AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22300",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Flow: the reported approximately 20% reduction over two weeks at unchanged valve settings matches the manual symptom 'Low flow or head'. The documented 300 m3/h at 45 m is the rated duty, not a minimum-flow, alarm or trip limit. Because neither the baseline nor present absolute flow is reported, the actual flow and any shortfall from rated flow cannot be calculated.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. On that measurement basis, 2.0 mm/s is within the 0.0-2.8 Zone A range ('New machines'), below the 2.8 Zone A/B boundary, below Zone C restricted operation at 4.5-7.1, and below Zone D at 7.1-11.0 where damage is likely and the chart says to stop the pump. It is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, so the site immediate-stop and reliability-engineer notification rule is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: applying the bearing-housing surface-temperature limits, 65 C is within 'Normal up to 70 C'; it is 5 C below the normal upper value, 15 C below the 80 C alarm and 25 C below the 90 C trip. Because it is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, the site requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift does not apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: no shaft-seal leakage is reported, so the manual's 'Leakage at shaft seal' troubleshooting row is not an active symptom. The service bulletin specifies which replacement seal and torque to use for this serial range; it does not direct an immediate proactive seal replacement solely because of the serial number.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn impeller: investigate first because it is the manual's first listed probable cause for low flow or head. Inspect the impeller and wear rings as directed; the reported gradual deterioration is consistent with investigating wear but does not confirm it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Air in suction: this is another documented probable cause of low flow or head. The manual's corrective action is to vent the casing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Closed valve: this remains a documented possible cause and should be checked physically. Unchanged valve settings do not provide an independent confirmation that the valves are presently open and effective.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Initially verify the actual suction and discharge valve status and use the manual low-flow corrective action to vent the casing for possible air in suction. Reassess flow at the existing valve settings before condemning internal parts.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If low flow persists and internal inspection is required, apply the isolation, line-break and lifting controls below. Use the HF-300 back pull-out arrangement to remove the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework, then inspect the impeller and wear rings. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If inspection confirms a worn impeller requiring replacement, install impeller HF3-210, 5-vane, 330 mm. If the M24 impeller nut is disturbed, tighten it to 160 Nm; Table 5's torque conditions are lightly oiled threads. Do not replace the impeller automatically without an inspection finding.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Whenever the casing is opened, install a new HF3-120 casing gasket. If M16 casing bolts are disturbed, tighten them to 210 Nm with lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If seal replacement becomes necessary, do not fit HF3-450. For serial HF3-22300 install pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B; no sleeve measurement is needed to set this seal. Tighten its seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, not the manual's superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "During applicable seal work, inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring and replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. The bulletin's 'no sleeve measurement' statement concerns setting the pre-set seal and does not remove this separate scoring check.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For return to service, maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. Record the resulting flow at the same valve settings and repeat the vibration and housing-temperature readings for comparison with the applicable manual limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; one required whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-210",
      "description": "Impeller, 5-vane, 330 mm; one only if inspection confirms that the worn-impeller cause requires replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; one if seal replacement is required. This is the mandatory substitute for HF3-450 on this serial-range pump and uses 30 Nm gland-nut torque.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; one if inspection during applicable seal work finds scoring deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Before any work inside the pump or on its seal, provide electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first. SSP-07 Rev 3 applies to all site pumps.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For lifting the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, the 25 kg threshold is exceeded: obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before line break, confirm P-112's line contents. Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory if its line is chemically dosed. The supplied sodium-hypochlorite information explicitly identifies P-101 to P-106, not P-112, so P-112's dosing status must not be guessed.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "No standard labour allowance is documented for the initial low-flow troubleshooting, back pull-out inspection, or impeller/wear-ring work. Table 6 does not list those scopes, so no inspection duration or total job duration is assigned here.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical-seal replacement, if authorised after inspection: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. This allowance is not by itself evidence that seal replacement is currently required.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection conflict: manual Revision D's parts list identifies HF3-450 as the component mechanical seal, while SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits fitting HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and requires cartridge HF3-450B. P-112 is serial HF3-22300 and therefore falls squarely within the bulletin range. Use HF3-450B if a seal is fitted; the manual part remains applicable only below the bulletin serial range. The bulletin decision is based on its explicit serial applicability, not an assumed issue date for the undated manual excerpt.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B and explicitly states that the previous value was 25 Nm. Because this asset is within the bulletin serial range and any replacement seal must be HF3-450B, 30 Nm governs that installation; do not use 25 Nm for the cartridge seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What are the baseline and present measured flow and head, and at what operating point were they taken? The 20% report cannot be converted to an absolute flow from the 300 m3/h at 45 m rating alone, and no low-flow acceptance, alarm or trip limit is supplied (C02, C09).",
    "Was the 2.0 mm/s vibration reading RMS and measured on a bearing housing, and was the 65 C reading taken on the bearing-housing surface? Those are the documented measurement bases for applying Figure 3 and the temperature limits; confirmation is required if the report used another method (C01, C02, C07).",
    "What are the impeller and wear-ring inspection findings and their acceptance/wear criteria? The troubleshooting table directs inspection but supplies no wear tolerance. If a wear ring requires replacement, its part number and quantity also need to be identified because it is absent from the supplied parts list (C05, C09).",
    "Does internal inspection establish any need for seal or shaft-sleeve work? No leakage is reported, so the current evidence does not establish seal failure; the conditional HF3-450B, 30 Nm and sleeve-scoring requirements apply if that work is performed (C09, C13).",
    "What labour allowance applies to diagnosis, back pull-out inspection and any impeller or wear-ring replacement? Table 6 provides times only for mechanical-seal replacement, bearing replacement and laser alignment (C12).",
    "Is P-112 on a chemically dosed line, and what is its process fluid? The evidence identifies sodium-hypochlorite dosing only for P-101 to P-106; if P-112 is also chemically dosed, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves must be added as applicable controls (C15, C16).",
    "What is the production consequence and required response time for the approximately 20% flow loss? The supplied site rules specify immediate-stop and P1 triggers for severe vibration and high bearing temperature but provide no P2/P3 mapping for flow degradation; P2 is therefore a planning judgement pending confirmation of process criticality (C07, C15)."
  ]
}
